WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.580
[Hank] Good morning, John.

00:00:00.580 --> 00:00:04.680
Parks and Rec was an extremely special television program.

00:00:04.780 --> 00:00:06.300
Not only was it hilarious,

00:00:06.300 --> 00:00:13.240
it was also friendly, and kind, and thoughtful, and full of people who disagreed, but enjoyed each other.

00:00:13.240 --> 00:00:15.880
And this is highlighted in a relationship between two main characters

00:00:15.880 --> 00:00:18.180
who could not disagree more, politically.

00:00:18.180 --> 00:00:21.140
[Leslie Knope] Government is bad.  Business is good. Free market... (mocking Ron)

00:00:21.140 --> 00:00:25.560
[Ron Swanson] (eating noises) Me want more pointless social programs, yummy, yummy, yum!

00:00:25.560 --> 00:00:28.960
[Hank] They disagree a lot. They disagree on politics, and on friendship...

00:00:28.960 --> 00:00:30.960
[Ron] I'm not interested in caring about people.

00:00:30.960 --> 00:00:32.960
[Hank] ...and weapons at work...

00:00:32.960 --> 00:00:35.400
[Ron] Literally everything is a weapon, son.

00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:36.400
[Hank] ...and marriage...

00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:39.480
[Ron] The reception will be held in each of our individual houses, alone.

00:00:39.480 --> 00:00:40.580
[Leslie] Pretend this is rice!

00:00:40.580 --> 00:00:44.040
[Hank] ...and they fight lots. But Leslie Knope and Ron Swanson do not hate each other.

00:00:44.180 --> 00:00:46.540
[Leslie] Hello, former strange person I used to friend.

00:00:46.740 --> 00:00:49.600
[Hank] Okay, they did for a little while, but mostly they don't.

00:00:49.600 --> 00:00:51.400
They have very different worldviews, but they are both,

00:00:51.400 --> 00:00:54.680
and this is important, and recognized by everyone who watches the show,

00:00:54.680 --> 00:00:55.960
*good people.*

00:00:56.100 --> 00:00:58.280
And they recognize each other's goodness.

00:00:58.280 --> 00:01:02.160
This is not "House of Cards," in which, as far as I can tell, there are no good people.

00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:07.020
The thing about Ron and Leslie is that their politics are far enough outside of the poisoned political discourse

00:01:07.020 --> 00:01:11.780
that they don't ever disagree about the classically politically charged issues of the day.

00:01:11.780 --> 00:01:17.080
Ron Swanson isn't a member of the NRA, probably, because he wouldn't give them his address.

00:01:17.080 --> 00:01:20.840
[Donna Meagle] Are you sure you want me to cut up *this* card? It gets you into the parking garage.

00:01:20.840 --> 00:01:23.920
[Ron] I'll be taking the bus now, and I'll be paying in cash.

00:01:23.920 --> 00:01:25.580
[Hank] This is a nice dramatic device because, of course,

00:01:25.580 --> 00:01:27.900
Ron doesn't believe that the government should regulate guns,

00:01:27.900 --> 00:01:31.600
but he also probably doesn't believe the government should regulate abortion or gay marriage,

00:01:31.600 --> 00:01:34.200
because he doesn't believe the government should regulate *anything*.

00:01:34.200 --> 00:01:40.280
[Ron] My idea of a perfect government is one guy who sits in a small room at a desk,

00:01:40.280 --> 00:01:42.660
and the only thing he's allowed to decide is who to nuke.

00:01:42.660 --> 00:01:45.340
[Hank] Likewise, Leslie is in the trenches of local government,

00:01:45.340 --> 00:01:47.900
and though she is clearly deeply progressive and liberal

00:01:47.900 --> 00:01:49.460
and a huge fan of Joe Biden...

00:01:49.460 --> 00:01:51.460
[Joe Biden] You must be Leslie Knope, welcome.

00:01:51.460 --> 00:01:53.140
[Leslie] (loud nervous laughter)

00:01:53.140 --> 00:01:55.560
[Hank] She isn't talking about gun control or immigration,

00:01:55.560 --> 00:01:57.560
she's just trying to make the Parks Department work.

00:01:57.740 --> 00:02:00.580
Which means that the politics of the show, while clearly liberal,

00:02:00.580 --> 00:02:05.120
are also disconnected from these extremely tense and seemingly intractable political debates,

00:02:05.120 --> 00:02:09.020
which makes it more believable that two people with such different belief systems

00:02:09.020 --> 00:02:10.520
could come to be close friends.

00:02:10.520 --> 00:02:11.880
[Leslie] Are we gonna hate each other someday?

00:02:11.880 --> 00:02:14.740
[Ron] I don't think so. I think we're gonna be fine.

00:02:14.740 --> 00:02:17.220
[Hank] But it says something about the discourse in the US right now

00:02:17.220 --> 00:02:19.520
that this distance from reality needs to be created

00:02:19.520 --> 00:02:24.100
in order to build a believable friendship between two people with different politics, even in a sitcom.

00:02:24.140 --> 00:02:30.320
It helps us believe that beneath it all there's something that works here and that thing, I think, is just respect.

00:02:30.560 --> 00:02:34.320
They value each other's convictions even though they always don't share the same goals,

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:37.900
and they almost never share the same opinions, except about breakfast food.

00:02:37.900 --> 00:02:40.400
[Leslie] Why would anybody ever eat anything besides breakfast food?!

00:02:40.400 --> 00:02:42.220
[Ron] People are idiots, Leslie.

00:02:42.420 --> 00:02:45.200
[Hank] Nowadays, there is so much more to the issues than the issues.

00:02:45.200 --> 00:02:48.620
An attack on a government policy or an inaction of a new policy

00:02:48.620 --> 00:02:52.360
can feel like an attack on our identity, an attack on *us*.

00:02:52.360 --> 00:02:56.520
But Ron and Leslie are able to move beyond that and share the world with each other,

00:02:56.520 --> 00:02:59.060
and they shared it respectfully, and with kindness,

00:02:59.060 --> 00:03:01.640
and the ability to value each other despite their differences.

00:03:01.640 --> 00:03:05.060
In the US, we're finding that harder and harder to do,

00:03:05.060 --> 00:03:07.980
and the deeper we get into this election season, the harder it's gonna get.

00:03:07.980 --> 00:03:12.020
We see the opposition, more than ever, both monolithically and negatively.

00:03:12.020 --> 00:03:15.860
You can live your entire life without knowing a single person

00:03:15.860 --> 00:03:18.340
who would even consider voting for the other side.

00:03:18.700 --> 00:03:20.840
We stay inside our bias-affirming filter,

00:03:20.840 --> 00:03:24.880
and think that anyone who disagrees with us must either be ignorant, or evil.

00:03:25.360 --> 00:03:28.300
It would be nice if we could all be a little bit more like Leslie and Ron,

00:03:28.460 --> 00:03:33.540
caring passionately about what we believe in without demonizing those who disagree with us.

00:03:33.540 --> 00:03:37.460
And never, never in my life has that been more difficult.

00:03:37.460 --> 00:03:39.460
John, I'll see you on Tuesday.

00:03:40.420 --> 00:03:41.520
(Loud saxophone honk)

